From f532dac4d91164085a9c5c80474f4a747af0308f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henry Wang <Henry.Wang@arm.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Aug 2023 14:52:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform/rss/kronos: Add Kronos board specific NI-710-AE
 driver

Refer to the Kronos Safety Island Architecture Specification,
use the NI-710-AE APU driver to configure the APUs from the
NI-710-AE interconnect.

The APU configuration is supposed to be two stages, i.e. the
boot time configuration where RSS/SCP is able to only see the
interfaces that they are supposed to touch. After the Safety Island
images are loaded, switch to the runtime APU configuration where
interfaces of Safety Island clusters are isolated.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Henry Wang <Henry.Wang@arm.com>
Signed-off-by: Wei Chen <wei.chen@arm.com>
